Do not send a client's own size back; fullscreen views keep the output size

Problem: when a client commits a size of its own, Wayfire adopts it and sends it
back in a configure. wlroots repeats that size in every later configure, so a
transient size sticks:
- Wine (winewayland) at scale 1.5 gets the fractional scale only after the first
  fullscreen configure, commits a stale 1707x960 once, and Deadlock stays at
  1707x960: not fullscreen, never scanned out. GNOME keeps the output size.
- Firefox/Thunderbird commit a transient small size and stay a "mini window"
  (upstream #3201).
Fix: (1) a client-initiated resize updates the size that wlroots repeats, but
sends no configure. (2) While the view is fullscreen, a commit of another size
is shown but not adopted: the view keeps the output size.
Upstream: same cause as https://github.com/WayfireWM/wayfire/issues/3201 (open;
the maintainer rejected a min-size clamp and asked why the small configure is
sent). Not reported by us. Draft: ~/Documents/Wayfire fullscreen stale size/.
Remove when: upstream main stops sending client-initiated sizes back and keeps
fullscreen sizes. Check: start Deadlock (PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1) at scale 1.5;
window-rules/list-views shows 2560x1440, not 1707x960.
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

